# Gate 6 (Architecture + Boy Scout) exemption.
#
# Why this project has no architecture.yaml
# ----------------------------------------
# pdf-translation is a flat two-module CLI, not a layered application:
#
#   pdf_translator.py   the translation engine
#   translate_pdf.py    the CLI entry point
#   test/               pytest suite
#
# There are no layers to order, no cross-layer imports to forbid, and no
# acyclic-dependency property worth asserting: `translate_pdf.py` imports
# `pdf_translator.py` and nothing else does. Writing a layers file here would
# be ceremony that enforces nothing while making Gate 6 report green -- the
# exact "taught users to write a file that bought them nothing" failure the
# gate's own hint warns about (xp-gate #686).
#
# Gate 6's layer-boundary enforcement is also inert in archlint 0.16.0, so even
# a correct-looking file would not be checked. This exemption records "not
# applicable" rather than pretending otherwise.
#
# Revisit if the project ever grows real modules with a direction of dependency
# (e.g. engines/, config/, cli/ with imports that must not point back upward).
# At that point delete this file and add architecture.yaml.
